    q: "A callable bond currently trades above par. Compared to its yield to maturity (YTM), its yield to call (YTC) is generally:",
    a: "Lower than the YTM, given the shorter period to the call",
    explanation: "Since a premium bond is typically called at or near par, the investor's premium loss is compressed into a shorter time frame, pulling the yield down versus holding to maturity. The yield falls because the built-in premium is recovered over a shorter period if the bond is called.",
