    explanation: "Rule 2a-7 imposes strict portfolio-level constraints — limiting holdings to high-quality, short-maturity, liquid instruments and capping the weighted average maturity of the portfolio — which is what allows those funds eligible to do so (government and retail money market funds) to seek a stable share price. Institutional prime and institutional tax-exempt funds must transact at a floating NAV, but remain subject to the same Rule 2a-7 portfolio constraints.",
