    q: "'Sequence of returns' risk is a distinctive concern for a retiree taking systematic withdrawals, but much less so for an accumulator making no withdrawals, because:",
    a: "With withdrawals, poor early returns do outsized damage, since each withdrawal comes from an already-depressed balance",
    explanation: "Two portfolios can earn the identical average annual return over the same span yet produce very different outcomes depending on the ORDER of those returns once cash is being withdrawn: selling into an early downturn permanently removes shares that would otherwise have participated in the later recovery, leaving less capital to recover.",
