    id: "s65-cl-x212",
    section: "client",
    q: "Unlike a two-asset portfolio's expected return, which is simply a weighted average of the two assets' expected returns, the portfolio's standard deviation:",
    a: "Also depends on the correlation coefficient between the two assets",
    explanation: "Portfolio risk is a function of each asset's weight and standard deviation AND the correlation between them. Because of this correlation term, portfolio standard deviation is generally less than the weighted average of the individual standard deviations (except in the special case of perfect positive correlation), which is the basis for diversification's risk-reduction benefit. Because of the correlation term, portfolio standard deviation generally cannot be found by weight-averaging the individual standard deviations.",
